# Optional. Without it the app still runs: interpretation falls back to the
# deterministic parser and narration to a fixed template (AGENTS.md invariant 13).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional, and used by `npx vitest run tests/conformance` only — never by the app.
# A Postgres connection string for the conformance suite's second adapter: a local
# server, a Supabase project, or any other Postgres. Supabase is Postgres, so the
# only thing that differs is this string.
#
#   local     postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/golden_analytics
#   Supabase  postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Unset, the suite runs one adapter and says loudly that the determinism claim is
# unproven on that run. Set but unreachable is a failure, not a skip.
#
# Never commit a real value here. The suite writes into a schema of its own,
# `golden_analytics_conformance`, and never touches `public`. It leaves the loaded
# data in place so a second run reuses it instead of re-uploading 132,628 rows, and
# says so on every run. To remove it:
#
#   DROP SCHEMA golden_analytics_conformance CASCADE;
CONFORMANCE_DATABASE_URL=
